  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The core Simoa and Spatial product lines are experiencing organic revenue declines, while overall top-line growth leans on contributions from diagnostics partnerships and recent acquisitions. The company is aggressively pivoting toward Alzheimer’s diagnostics, building momentum through a Tempus AI collaboration, new assay launches, and a planned FDA submission for LucentAD Complete in late 2026. This shift reflects a targeted bet on the high-need neurology diagnostics market, though legacy research-tool demand remains under pressure.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** New CEO Everett Cunningham is steering a strategic transformation with a sharpened focus on commercial scale, return on investment, and diagnostics leadership. The team is investing in lab infrastructure, hiring a diagnostics head, and pursuing regulatory clearance, while capturing substantial cost synergies from the Akoya integration that are improving adjusted EBITDA. With a debt-free balance sheet and maintained full-year guidance, management is projecting a steadier, cash-conscious path through the transition, though execution credibility remains mixed amid prior earnings misses.",
